\section{API token}{

All API functions need an access token, which you can get at
\url{https://www.ean-search.org/ean-database-api.html}. Set it in the
environment variable \code{EAN_SEARCH_API_TOKEN} (eg. in \code{.Renviron}) or pass
it to each function as \code{token}.
}

\section{Errors}{

Network and API errors do not raise R errors: lookups return \code{NA} or
\code{NULL}, searches return an empty data frame, and \code{\link[=eansearch_error]{eansearch_error()}} tells
what went wrong. Requests rejected with HTTP status 429 (too many requests)
are retried up to 3 times.
}

\section{Options}{

\itemize{
\item \code{eansearch.timeout}: HTTP timeout in seconds (default 30).
\item \code{eansearch.useragent}: HTTP user agent (default \verb{r-eansearch/<version>}).
}
